# Story page: hunt
# {name} becomes the snake's name. Paragraphs are separated by a blank line.
title = Hunting Grounds
---
In the long grass something else was moving, and it was moving the way {name} moved.

It was a snake, dark as a bruise, with eyes like two coins. It ate {name}'s apples. Then it looked at {name} the way {name} looks at apples.

{name} learned two things that day. That a body can be a wall. And that a skin, once shed, makes a better one. The Hunter learned only one thing, which was 'ow', three times.
